{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "1. Find your exposed listing",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C1",
      "text": "1. Search the people-search site for your name, phone number, or address and open the listing that appears to describe you.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Submit the opt-out",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C2",
      "text": "1. Use the site's opt-out or removal instructions for the listing you found and complete the requested steps.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Repeat across sites",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C3",
      "text": "1. Move to the next relevant people-search site and repeat the same search-and-opt-out workflow.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Recheck periodically",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C4",
      "text": "[ ] Schedule a periodic recheck and submit another opt-out request if your information appears again.",
      "type": "bullet"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Know the limits",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C5",
      "text": "Note: Treat this as exposure reduction, not total erasure: public records may still remain available.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C6",
      "text": "DIY opt-outs can be done for free; a paid service is an alternative if you prefer to delegate the repeated work.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ],
